From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A shader whose SPIR-V the driver refuses builds no pipeline,
 rather than crashing it

This War of Mine crashed on a VkPipelineBuilder thread (SIGSEGV at 0x40, radv_shader_spirv_to_nir,
radv_shader.c:539, read with 5.0.1's eden.elf): Mesa's spirv_to_nir refused one of its shaders as Eden
translated it and gave back nothing, which RADV used. Why it was refused went to the debug-report
callback Eden does not install.

tools/patch-radv-spirv-failure.py, applied to the driver after the other four: the reason goes to
stderr (stderr.log) with the stage, and a graphics or compute pipeline with such a shader fails with
VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN. Eden already logs a pipeline that fails and skips the draws and dispatches that use
it. Its stamp, EDEN_SPIRV_FAILURE_SHA256, rebuilds a driver built without it; check-radv-gs-cache.py
knows it.
---
 tools/build-radv-dependencies.sh  |   2 +
 tools/check-radv-gs-cache.py      |   5 +
 tools/patch-radv-spirv-failure.py | 151 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/prepare-build.sh            |   3 +-
 4 files changed, 160 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100755 tools/patch-radv-spirv-failure.py

